  8	// Its due-total is the sum of the people's figures for it. A period can be closed: each person's figure
  9	// is then the one fixed at closing. It can instead be soft-closed: the figures are fixed the same way
 10	// but its claims can still change; a soft-closed period can then be closed or reopened. A permitted role (a steward by default) can reopen a
 11	// closed period, making its due-total live again. A second form generates a period per calendar month
 12	// over a range of dates, named yyyy-mm, leaving out months whose name is taken or that overlap a period;
 13	// a third does the same for the twelve months of a fiscal year. Each period shows the fiscal year its
 14	// from-date falls in. A period may cap the OPEN or PENDING claims due by in it each person may have.
